{"kind":"event","event_id":8670,"event_uid":"01M2Q31K8Z35YH29AJ4RMR9N22","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":359,"issue_uid":"01M2Q2XBDZPM2TG1VPH9RT3SN5","issue_short_id":"3sn5","actor":"exam:1@run-174","hlc_physical_ms":1789628828959,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"7318765f1a992bfbd144de069dfc11f7e1e8aac689b4d955c4eb1083da9887b6","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q31K8X721DKP6XKQJ6ZGVP","author":"exam:1@run-174","body":"examiner (exam round 1): approach for the exam at `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_own_proofs.mjs`.\n\nExtending the file under a new section marker `Task 1 (2026-09-17, #1100)`, the way the existing `Task 3 (2026-09-17)` marker does; everything above it is left byte-for-byte as it stands.\n\nFour new scenarios, one per Proof leg:\n\n- S13 — legs (a) and (b) [M1, M2]. The S1 scenario shape (one task, `proofTests: ['t1_test.sh']`, a `testCmd`, two `proofRuns` of which the second is red on the implementer's tree and green after the fix round) so one run records `impl:T1`, `exam:T1`, `fix:T1:0` and `review:T1:1`. The task's `mkTask` entry gets `body: undefined`; the launch file is written under the sim's temp root with `tasks: [{ id: 'T1', body: BODY_LAUNCH, ... }]` and reaches `runEngine` through the rig's `extraArgs.wavesPath`. Each of the four prompts is asserted, one label at a time, to contain `'\\\\nTASK:\\\\n' + BODY_LAUNCH` as a substring; each is separately asserted not to contain the pointer phrase.\n- S14 — leg (c) [M3]. A second run with `body` inline and no `wavesPath`: `impl:T2` and `review:T2:1` each contain `'\\\\nTASK:\\\\n' + BODY`, and none of that run's prompts carries the pointer phrase either (leg (b)'s second half).\n- S15 — leg (d) [M4]. A launch file whose `tasks` array holds only `T9` while the wave's body-less task is `T3`: `await assert.rejects(run(), ...)` on a message containing both `T3` and the launch file's path, and the stub recorded no label at all.\n- S16 — leg (e) [M5]. The source-level half of the Proof's second `Run:`: `test_resolver_brief.mjs` is still there and still ends in the `ALL TESTS PASSED` sentinel that `Run:` greps for, plus a direct equality on `waveContendingBlock`'s BASE render (it is pure and exported, so the exam can pin the `wavesPath` sentence byte for byte rather than only pin the sim that pins it).\n- Plus the first `Run:` transliterated: zero lines of `fleet/run-engine.mjs` carry the phrase `read your verbatim task text` [M2].\n\nReading recorded for leg (d): the stub in S15 records its label and returns a benign reply rather than throwing, so that at BASE (where no rejection happens) the failure reads as `assert.rejects` finding no rejection, not as a stub error whose text happens to contain `T3`.","created_at":"2026-09-17T07:07:08.957849530Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T07:07:08.959Z"}
