{"kind":"event","event_id":8770,"event_uid":"01M2Q38DT5GYKEW0M7WZDPF97C","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":359,"issue_uid":"01M2Q2XBDZPM2TG1VPH9RT3SN5","issue_short_id":"3sn5","actor":"impl:1@run-174","hlc_physical_ms":1789629052741,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"6980e6b4efdbb6d1992c09a7771b0cba1e6e1ae574c275a5c472fe6030aefe04","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q38DT3S08R3NCJ4PRE5R88","author":"impl:1@run-174","body":"Done at 31b807eb. runEngine loads args.wavesPath once right after wavesPath is computed (run-engine.mjs), indexes launch.tasks by id, fills task.body for every body-less WAVES entry, then throws 'run-engine: task <id> has no body: not inline in args.waves and not in <wavesPath>' for any task still bodyless — before any dispatch. taskBodyBlock is now one line, inline branch only, and takes just (task); the three call sites (impl/exam shared inputs, fix round, reviewer) drop the wavesPath argument. waveContendingBlock, the args.json key and makeAddDirsFor are untouched.\n\nVerified behaviourally with a throwaway rig script (written in-tree, run, deleted — not committed): M1 the four labels impl:T1/exam:T1/fix:T1:0/review:T1:1 are all recorded and each prompt contains '\\nTASK:\\n'+BODY for a body-less task whose body is only in the launch file; M2 none of them contains the pointer phrase and grep -c on run-engine.mjs is 0; M3 an inline-body run with no wavesPath still renders impl:T2 and review:T2:1 the same way; M4 a launch file whose tasks names only T9 while the wave's body-less task is T3 rejects with a message containing both T3 and the path, with no label recorded. M5 is the resolver brief sim, green.\n\nAll 21 test_run_engine_*.mjs sims plus test_resolver_brief, test_launch_*, test_publish_fold, test_facts_block and test_sims_are_hermetic pass on the patched tree.\n\nOrdering note a later session may want: the new bodyless throw fires before the args.patchInput and args.testCmd checks, since it sits at the wavesPath load. No sim depends on which of those throws first.\n\nI did not write fleet/tests/test_run_engine_own_proofs.mjs — that path is the peer examiner's, laid over at handoff.","created_at":"2026-09-17T07:10:52.739388845Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T07:10:52.741Z"}
